# run-suites.quarantine -- suites that still run and still print, but do not
# gate. Tab-separated: <suite path>\t<issue>\t<why>
#
# THIS IS THE HONEST LEVER, and the only one. The alternative when a suite
# is red on the day a `tests` check lands is to edit the suite until CI
# opens green, which is the exact move BUILD-DISCIPLINE.md exists to
# prevent. A line here says "known red, tracked, not gating" out loud and
# names the issue that closes it.
#
# It SHRINKS. run-suites.sh prints a ::notice when a quarantined suite
# passes, so a stale line announces itself rather than quietly forgiving a
# suite that no longer needs it.
#
# READ THE NOTICE WHERE IT FIRED. hf7y/senechal#465 measured the #407 block
# that used to sit here directly on this runner (monkey): all four suites
# passed. Three were already hermetic and simply mislabeled; the fourth
# (tools/test-vault.sh) had a real fixture bug -- `git init --bare` points
# HEAD at refs/heads/master regardless of what gets pushed, so a clone of a
# freshly-seeded origin checked out nothing on a host without
# init.defaultBranch=main, fixed in the same change that removed this
# block. A "stale, remove its line" notice from run-suites.sh IS the
# runner talking; believe it over a comment that predates the check.
#
# NOT LISTED, on purpose: test/contract-test.sh. That is a harness, not a
# suite -- it takes <command-under-test> as an argument and exits 2 with a
# usage error when globbed in bare. CI invokes it as
# `test/contract-test.sh bin/installe`, which passes 7/7. Quarantining it
# would hide a green check behind a word that means "broken".

test/lance-test.sh	699	bin/lance was reversed out 2026-09-05 (Zach's #699 DECISION: the 2026-08-27 reap order #405/#590 quietly undone stands) -- the suite exercises a binary that no longer exists
test/debarrasse-test.sh	699	bin/debarrasse was reversed out 2026-09-05 (Zach's #699 DECISION: the 2026-08-27 reap order #405/#590 quietly undone stands) -- the suite exercises a binary that no longer exists
